from pathlib import Path
import json,numpy as np,matplotlib
matplotlib.use('Agg')
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
O=Path(__file__).parent;rows=json.loads((O/'effective-bank-ablation.json').read_text());x=np.arange(8);fig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(12,4.5),layout='constrained')
for i,(r,c) in enumerate(zip(rows,['#8294a3','#c87945','#178389'])):ax.bar(x+(i-1)*.25,r['validation_rmse_by_window_deg'],.25,label=r['case'].replace('_',' ').capitalize(),color=c)
ax.set_xticks(x,['HR 447','HR 450','HR 508','HR 400','TL 326','TL 402','TL 3387','TL 290']);ax.set_ylabel('Bank prediction RMS error (deg)');ax.set_title('The inferred brake dead zone helps Hood River but hurts Trout Lake\nLower is better · identical training windows and prediction horizons');ax.legend(fontsize=9);ax.grid(axis='y',alpha=.2);ax.spines[['top','right']].set_visible(False);fig.savefig(O/'iteration-bank-ablation.png',dpi=160)
p=O/'physics-development.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s=s.replace('</html>','''<h2>Brake-threshold ablation</h2><figure><img src="iteration-bank-ablation.png" alt="Validation error with no brake threshold, shared threshold, and asymmetric thresholds"><figcaption>The asymmetric threshold improves the Hood River high-bank development cases but worsens all four displayed Trout Lake cases. It is not established as a transferable hardware dead zone. Removing the threshold gives much better Trout Lake predictions but misses the Hood River turn. Separate per-flight fits reduce training errors while worsening several withheld predictions, so configuration-specific fitting is not an accepted fix either.</figcaption></figure><p>Results: <code>effective-bank-ablation.json</code> and <code>effective-bank-per-flight.json</code>. This tradeoff must remain visible alongside the promising first bank plot. Next work must fit a broader range of excitation and couple speed/climb to the bank dynamics before selecting the final model.</p></html>''');p.write_text(s)
